length of the array. Let=E2=80=99s see how we could do better.</p>
<p>It=E2=80=99s important to understand that every number in the array can =
represent the start of some consecutive chain. One approach is to treat eac=
h number as the start of a chain and search through the array to identify t=
he rest of its chain.</p>
<p>To do this, we can leverage the fact that for any number <code>num</code=
>, its next consecutive number will be <code>num + 1</code>. This means we=
=E2=80=99ll always know which number to look for when trying to find the ne=
xt number in a sequence. The code snippet for this approach is provided bel=
